          "section": "2. Experimental procedure",
          "quote": "Two HEAs were melted from pure metals (purity > 99.8 wt%) by Vacuum Arc Re-melting (VAR) technique. Carbon powder was wrapped in pure Fe before melting to completely dissolve the carbon inside the melt. Also, an additional Mn (10 wt%) was added to each ingot to compensate for the evaporation due to its relatively high vapour pressure. Re-melting and homogenisation at 1200 °C for 24 h (in argon) were carried out to enhance the homogeneity of chemical composition.",
